  aiChatHelpAria: "About the AI chat controls",
  aiChatHelpPasteHtml: "<strong>AI chat \u2014 copy &amp; paste mode</strong> (no AI credentials)<br>Write a message and use <strong>Copy prompt</strong>, paste it into your external AI, then <strong>Import AI answer\u2026</strong>.<br><strong>Prompts \u25BE</strong> stored prompts: insert, save or remove reusable texts.<br><strong>Trash</strong> clears this project's chat history. Then also start a new chat in your external AI and paste the full prompt again: the next copied prompt automatically includes the full project context.<br><strong>Toggle</strong> (right) collapses or expands the chat; the state is remembered.<br><strong>Context chips</strong>: right-click source nodes, target nodes or blocks \u2192 <em>Add to AI chat</em>.<br><strong>Notes / Questions</strong> from the AI show in a yellow box; <em>Answer</em> quotes a question into the input. A <strong>NN%</strong> badge and dashed outline mark low-confidence suggestions on blocks; edit or right-click \u2192 <em>Mark as reviewed</em> to clear.<br><strong>AI credentials</strong> (menu <em>AI \u2192 Configure AI credentials\u2026</em>) connect an API so the chat can send directly.",
  aiChatHelpApiHtml: "<strong>AI chat \u2014 API mode</strong><br><strong>Send</strong> talks to your configured AI. The first message carries a compact project context (slot manifest, source paths, example list; the AI fetches more with its tools); later ones only your text and new context chips.<br><strong>Prompts \u25BE</strong> stored prompts: insert, save or remove reusable texts.<br><strong>Streaming</strong>: the answer and any model reasoning stream in as they arrive; each mapping the AI applies through its mapping tools shows as a short \u2713 line. Changes land on the canvas right away; <em>Revert last AI turn</em> undoes the whole turn.<br><strong>Stop</strong> (or Esc in the input) ends a run that seems to go wrong; mappings made before Stop stay and can be reverted.<br><strong>Trash</strong> clears this project's chat history and starts a fresh context: the next message resends the full project context.<br><strong>Toggle</strong> (right) collapses or expands the chat; the state is remembered.<br><strong>Context chips</strong>: right-click source nodes, target nodes or blocks \u2192 <em>Add to AI chat</em>.<br><strong>Notes / Questions</strong> from the AI show in a yellow box; <em>Answer</em> quotes a question into the input. A <strong>NN%</strong> badge and dashed outline mark low-confidence suggestions on blocks; edit or right-click \u2192 <em>Mark as reviewed</em> to clear.<br><strong>AI credentials</strong> (menu <em>AI \u2192 Configure AI credentials\u2026</em>) change provider, key or model.",
